Adapted files (package com.claudechat.phone):
  McpServer.java  from app/buddy/assistant/McpServer.java: local MCP server on 127.0.0.1:8765
  Tools.java      from app/buddy/assistant/Tools.java: the phone tools (read_screen, tap, type_text, scroll, ...)
  PhoneService.java  from app/buddy/assistant/BuddyService.java: accessibility service that hosts the server

Written for Claude Chat, not copied: ConfirmActivity.java (approval dialog, in place of the upstream bubble),
PhoneControl.java (switch and token), and the resource files phone_access.xml and the phone_* / confirm_* strings.

Changes from upstream: no bubble overlay, chat hub, onboarding, Termux helper endpoints, attachment endpoint,
lock-screen handling or keyboard tracking. Approvals are a dialog, status is a toast and the control notice is a
plain notification. Each adapted Java file carries a header that says so.
